From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <89942958+henrikklee@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:45:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] storage: Add read-only NVMe for A9 and A10 behind apcie

On A9 and A10, ANS is an NVMe endpoint behind the apcie (H8P/H9P) PCIe
root complex and the ADT has no /arm-io/ans, so main_storage_init()
reported storage as unsupported. Add a backend for apcie,t8010 and
apcie,s8003: power apcie, set up the root complex and port 0, the NVMMU
with its SART aperture onto the ADT host memory buffer, the queues behind
dart-apcie0 and data through NVMMU FlatDMA, following Linux's
pcie-apple-h9p.c and pci-apple-ans.c. Registers, pins and the HMB come
from the ADT; the SoC differences (common init, port 0 power cycle and
link start, NVMMU invalidate FIFO, L1SS value, GPIO function) are per-SoC
data. S8000 (A9, Samsung) has a different root complex and isn't covered.

The backend has no write path. Shutdown stops the controller the way
iBoot does, then clears and masks the port interrupt before taking the
port down and powering apcie off. A pending link event left in the port
interrupt status makes Linux's port interrupt storm.

chainload_load() now uses the generic main storage functions, like the
Rust side already does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
