+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT */
+/*
+ * Read-only NVMe for A9 (S8003) and A10 (T8010), where ANS is an NVMe
+ * endpoint behind the apcie (H8P/H9P) PCIe root complex instead of an
+ * ASC-attached controller.
+ *
+ * The bring-up follows Linux's pcie-apple-h9p.c and pci-apple-ans.c: the
+ * SoC's root complex and port 0 setup, NVMMU with the SART aperture onto
+ * the ADT host memory buffer, queues behind dart-apcie0, data through
+ * NVMMU FlatDMA. The shutdown leaves the port the way Linux expects to find
+ * it after power-on reset: the controller stopped the way iBoot stops it,
+ * the port interrupt cleared and masked, the port down and apcie off.
+ */
+
